# ProjectOS — agent rules (Cursor; mirrors the root CLAUDE.md)

Before executing ANY task:
1. Read, in order: docs/00_Baseline_State.md, docs/01_PRD.md, docs/02_AppFlow.md, docs/03_UI_Spec.md,
   docs/04_TRD.md, docs/05_Schema.md, docs/06_Plan.md.
2. If the task changes code, read docs/changes/delta_spec.md (or write one first): ADDED / MODIFIED /
   PROTECTED. Show it and wait for owner approval before writing code.
3. Never modify a file listed as PROTECTED in docs/00_Baseline_State.md §4 or in the delta spec
   without explicit owner approval.
4. After every completed step, update docs/06_Plan.md: tick the box, and add the date, the commit and
   one line of evidence.

Working rules (owner directive, unchanged):
- FIX IT, OR SAY THE FIX. Within permission, fix it and report. Outside permission, name the concrete
  fix, who must take it, and what it costs. Never return "blocked" as the whole answer.
- Protected actions always stop and ask: production deployment; production or destructive database
  mutation; real email, SMS or messaging; payments; credential disclosure or rotation; service
  installation; ACL, registry or ProgramData changes; destructive machine operations; force push;
  merge; push; phase closure; anything a gate withheld.
- Use the locked stack in docs/04_TRD.md. Use the design tokens in docs/03_UI_Spec.md; never invent
  values.
- Every new rule gets a validator pin and a named mutation. Tests sit beside their peers.
